From: TheMoon <execorvo@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: drop the menu governor, keep teo only

Removes CONFIG_CPU_IDLE_GOV_MENU from the GKI defconfig, leaving teo
as the only cpuidle governor. teo generally makes better idle-state
predictions than menu on modern hardware; there's no reason to carry
both when only one will actually be selected as default anyway.

Applies to: kernel-6.6/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
index 4e687735adeb..1111111111 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
@@ -79,7 +79,6 @@ CONFIG_PM_DEBUG=y
 CONFIG_PM_ADVANCED_DEBUG=y
 CONFIG_ENERGY_MODEL=y
 CONFIG_CPU_IDLE=y
-CONFIG_CPU_IDLE_GOV_MENU=y
 CONFIG_CPU_IDLE_GOV_TEO=y
 CONFIG_ARM_PSCI_CPUIDLE=y
 CONFIG_CPU_FREQ=y
